{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:41:41Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 98, "kind": "message", "text": "`docs/spec.md` is written for Taiga #12 (branch `feature/tp-12/give-tasks-due-date`, workspace already clean and on the correct branch \u2014 no hygiene issue to resolve).\n\n**Summary of the spec:**\n- **Feature**, sized like the existing priority feature (#4) \u2014 same shape, one cycle, no story split needed.\n- Optional `due_date` (date-only, no time) on create and per-row edit, mirroring how `priority` already works: new `DueDateIn` model, `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/due-date`, `store.set_due_date()`.\n- 9 falsifiable acceptance criteria, including the two real product calls I made a default decision on rather than leaving open:\n  1. \"Overdue\" = strictly before today, not including today.\n  2. Marking a task done suppresses its overdue indicator, regardless of stored date.\n  Both are flagged as small, reversible defaults in Open Questions if the human wants them flipped.\n- Explicit non-goals: no sort/filter by due date, no time-of-day, no reminders/recurrence, no timezone handling.\n- AC4 calls out the accessibility constraint from the request directly: overdue must be marked by something other than colour alone (text/icon), with exact visual treatment left to ux-designer.\n- Affected areas listed with exact file/line references on both backend and frontend, following the priority feature as the concrete precedent throughout.\n\nI overwrote the previous cycle's `docs/spec.md` (Taiga #11, search by title) \u2014 that ticket is already merged (`7c1276f`/`5e852f6`), so this is normal per-cycle scratch turnover, not clobbering unmerged work.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "68bbec07-96f9-46a1-a6cf-f23842d6dfe3"}}
